new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/engineering/paperdiy.md
@@ -0,0 +1,102 @@
+# M5Stack PaperDIY experimental port
+
+Status: local development target. CrossMux has not been flashed or accepted on
+the device yet. The donor CrossPoint PaperDIY build passed boot, SD, reading,
+buttons and menu smoke tests on this user's unit; that evidence does not validate
+this CrossMux binary. Sleep current is unmeasured.
+
+## Hardware and route
+
+The M5Stack K159 PaperDIY uses an ESP32-S3 N16R8, 16MB DIO Flash, 8MB OPI PSRAM,
+and a parallel ED047TC1 960x540 panel. SD is SPI SCLK39/MISO40/MOSI38/CS47.
+Buttons A/B are GPIO4/GPIO3. M5PM1 is at I2C 0x6e on SDA41/SCL42; PYG2 supplies
+the panel and PYG3 is active-low charge status. There is no touch, frontlight,
+RTC, IMU or audio in this profile. See the
+[vendor pin map](https://docs.m5stack.com/en/core/PaperDIY_Assembly_Kit).
+
+CrossMux base: `a78a39ed04d6755c6885d57521704d2f96f8b955`.
+SDK base: `9aa7e95e02c6374a23a562c883eb302552ff24f1` from `0x1abin/freeink-sdk`.
+PaperDIY changes are adapted from `prateek/freeink-sdk` commit
+`5663993f2c69a28efaddaefb7e4bf9e9899ef229` and `prateek/crosspoint-reader`
+commit `268216cdc3f5e7c5a016f476f57fa26d75047ebb`.
+
+Keep the configured SDK gitlink: the working SDK contains a local patch, not an
+integrated SDK release. Reproduction requires both firmware and SDK patches;
+an ordinary recursive clone of this base does not include PaperDIY support.
+The port adds a board profile, PMIC/button/battery wiring and display config
+selection. It retains CrossMux's existing display driver, renderer, applications,
+storage and BLE interfaces. Existing Board enum values are preserved.
+
+## Build and checks
+
+After applying both recorded patches to their bases:
+
+```sh
+python -m pip install pioarduino==6.2.0
+python scripts/patch_pioarduino_cache.py --prepare-platform
+pio run -e paperdiy
+sh freeink-sdk/libs/hardware/InputManager/test/host/run_paperdiy.sh
+python test/test_paperdiy_board_tag.py
+python test/test_hal_power_sources.py
+./bin/ci-check
+```
+
+The target uses the prebuilt `dio_opi` core, existing S3 PSRAM BLE configuration,
+and application LTO. The pinned M5GFX commit is
+`d8074bbac8b75d22149d128d71d55b6a34dbc808`. Outputs are
+`.pio/build/paperdiy/firmware.bin` (application) and `firmware.factory.bin`
+(merged installation). Build and test results are pending and will be recorded
+in the handoff report with hashes and logs.
+
+The board tag is `paperdiy`; tagged images for other boards are rejected by the
+existing scanner. This target is not enrolled in release/OTA indexes. Do not
+use another target's OTA binary or assume an SDK-only PaperS3 profile is usable.
+
+## Input and power contract
+
+- Tap A: Up / previous page; hold A: Back.
+- Tap B: Down / next page; hold B: Confirm / menu.
+- Hold both: logical Power, using the existing two-button classifier.
+- The PMIC click is a one-shot logical Power event. Default Ignore retains
+  shutdown behavior; explicit alternate short-power bindings still apply.
+- Shutdown requests M5PM1 power-off. If USB retains power, turn off the panel
+  rail, wait for A/B release, then arm either key as a deep-sleep wake source.
+- USB cold boots stay awake. External supply detection is distinct from charge
+  status, including when the battery is full.
+
+No new framebuffer or dynamic allocation is introduced by the board plumbing.
+Its 64,800-byte facade framebuffer is in PSRAM; M5GFX, fonts and BLE have their
+own allocations. Actual internal/PSRAM heap peaks must be measured on-device.
+
+## Physical acceptance still pending
+
+Preserve verified original Flash backups and obtain approval for this specific
+new image before flashing. Match COM identity, image hash and offsets first.
+Back up SD settings/progress before testing a different reader fork.
+
+Validate boot identity, 8MB runtime PSRAM, SD mount and visible panel output;
+all four orientations, text/grayscale refresh and input during refresh;
+A/B short/held gestures, popup release barriers and sleep/wake on battery/USB;
+EPUB/TXT opening, cross-chapter turns and progress after restart. Test Apps
+individually: two physical keys do not establish that every game's controls
+are usable. Measure current before making battery-life claims. CrossMux-specific
+Apps, standby faces and BLE acceptance are separate from donor reader tests.
+
+## Initial physical findings and next candidate
+
+The first candidate passed boot, SD/fonts, EPUB page turns and reader menu checks
+on this unit. Home Apps selection exposed a shared home-menu bug with installed
+plugins and no OPDS servers: rendering omitted the plugin slot while activation
+included it. Rendering now uses the same hasLibrarySlot() condition.
+
+The panel photo showed old reading text on the home background, while a serial
+framebuffer capture had clean white pixels there. Manual forced refresh visibly
+cleared the residue. Repeated home-menu fast updates also accumulated ghosting.
+The next candidate therefore queues one full refresh on PaperDIY reader exit and
+uses a PaperDIY-only UI budget: three normal-context fast paints, then one clean
+paint. Four is an experimental physical-test cadence, not a calibrated optimum.
+Continuous-reading/AA/image contexts keep their existing reader cadence. Explicit
+Half/Full requests are retained; failed commits do not consume a due cleanup.
+The budget adds one static byte and no allocation. Existing panel waveforms and
+SDK display driver code are unchanged. Ghosting acceptance is pending this new
+candidate's physical tests; the initial image is not accepted for UI cleanliness.
diff --git a/lib/hal/PaperDiyRefreshBudget.h b/lib/hal/PaperDiyRefreshBudget.h
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/lib/hal/PaperDiyRefreshBudget.h
@@ -0,0 +1,27 @@
+#pragma once
+
+#include <stdint.h>
+
+// Experimental PaperDIY UI cadence: cap successive fast menu paints at three,
+// then use the clean refresh already verified on this panel. Reader refresh
+// contexts keep their own page cadence. One byte of state, no allocation.
+class PaperDiyRefreshBudget {
+ public:
+  static constexpr uint8_t FAST_UI_LIMIT = 4;
+
+  bool needsClean(bool fast, bool normalContext) const {
+    return fast && normalContext && fastUiPaints >= FAST_UI_LIMIT - 1;
+  }
+
+  void completed(bool fast, bool normalContext, bool committed) {
+    if (!committed) return;
+    if (!fast) {
+      fastUiPaints = 0;
+    } else if (normalContext && fastUiPaints < FAST_UI_LIMIT) {
+      ++fastUiPaints;
+    }
+  }
+
+ private:
+  uint8_t fastUiPaints = 0;
+};
diff --git a/test/test_paperdiy_board_tag.py b/test/test_paperdiy_board_tag.py
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/test/test_paperdiy_board_tag.py
@@ -0,0 +1,39 @@
+"""Compile the production board scanner for PaperDIY and reject other targets."""
+from pathlib import Path
+import subprocess
+import tempfile
+
+ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]
+
+with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory(prefix="paperdiy-tag-") as directory:
+    work = Path(directory)
+    (work / "BoardConfig.h").write_text("#define FREEINK_DEVICE_PAPERDIY 1\n")
+    (work / "check.cpp").write_text(r'''
+#include <FirmwareBoardTag.h>
+#include <cassert>
+#include <cstring>
+int main() {
+  assert(board_tag::boardNameLen() == std::strlen("paperdiy"));
+  assert(std::memcmp(board_tag::boardName(), "paperdiy", 8) == 0);
+  const char* tags[] = {"CROSSPOINT-BOARD-V1:paperdiy;",
+                        "CROSSPOINT-BOARD-V1:m5paper_s3;",
+                        "CROSSPOINT-BOARD-V1:papermono;",
+                        "CROSSPOINT-BOARD-V1:x4;"};
+  for (unsigned i = 0; i < 4; ++i) {
+    for (size_t split = 0; split <= std::strlen(tags[i]); ++split) {
+      board_tag::Scanner scanner;
+      auto bytes = reinterpret_cast<const uint8_t*>(tags[i]);
+      scanner.feed(bytes, split);
+      scanner.feed(bytes + split, std::strlen(tags[i]) - split);
+      assert(scanner.mismatch() == (i != 0));
+    }
+  }
+}
+''')
+    executable = work / "check"
+    subprocess.run(["c++", "-std=c++17", "-Wall", "-Wextra", "-Werror",
+                    f"-I{work}", f"-I{ROOT / 'src/network'}",
+                    str(ROOT / "src/network/FirmwareBoardTag.cpp"),
+                    str(work / "check.cpp"), "-o", str(executable)], check=True)
+    subprocess.run([str(executable)], check=True)
+print("PaperDIY board identity and wrong-board rejection passed")
